CAT = "rshairSafety"; SEG = "SAF"
# RSOS tasks A-1 (safety-related and hygienic functions) and A-2 (tools and equipment).
Q = [
("A comb has hair and gel on it. What must happen before it goes into disinfectant?",
 "Wash off the debris", ["Rinse it in hot water only", "Spray it with sanitizer", "Leave it to air-dry"],
 "Disinfectant cannot reach a surface under hair and product, so the tool is cleaned with soap and water first. Rinsing or spraying alone leaves the residue in place."),
("Which describes disinfecting, as opposed to cleaning, sanitizing or sterilizing?",
 "Destroys most microbes on tools", ["Removes only visible dirt", "Kills all microbes and spores", "Lowers microbes on fabrics"],
 "Disinfecting destroys most microbes on hard tools and surfaces. Cleaning removes dirt, sanitizing lowers microbe counts on items such as towels and capes, and only sterilizing kills spores."),
("A disinfectant jar looks cloudy with floating hair before its scheduled change. What now?",
 "Replace it now", ["Strain out the hair", "Add fresh concentrate", "Change it at day's end"],
 "The RSOS has the solution replaced to keep its disinfecting strength. Cloudy, contaminated solution is changed at once, not topped up or strained."),
("A new case of lightener arrives. Which WHMIS label must its original container carry?",
 "Supplier label", ["Workplace label", "Laboratory label", "Shipping manifest"],
 "Hazardous products arrive with a supplier label from the maker or importer. A workplace label is needed only when the product is moved into another container."),
("On a WHMIS label, which hazard does a flame over a circle warn of?",
 "An oxidizer", ["A flammable liquid", "An explosive", "A corrosive"],
 "The flame-over-circle pictogram marks oxidizing products, which feed a fire with oxygen. A plain flame marks flammables and a corrosion symbol marks corrosives."),
("Where does a used straight-razor blade go?",
 "Into a sharps container", ["Into a covered waste can", "Into the disinfectant jar", "Into a recycling bin"],
 "Blades are infectious material and are discarded in a puncture-resistant sharps container. A covered waste can protects against odour, not against a needle-stick or cut."),
("A client is nicked and bleeds. What does the stylist put on before touching the wound?",
 "Disposable gloves", ["A face mask only", "Safety glasses only", "A cotton neck strip"],
 "Blood is handled with gloves to protect both people, then the area is treated with first aid and contaminated items are bagged. Glasses or a cape do not guard the hands."),
("Lightener splashes into a client's eye. Which safety equipment is used first?",
 "Eyewash station", ["First aid kit eye pad", "Neutralizing shampoo", "Cool damp towel"],
 "The eye is flushed at once with plenty of water at an eyewash station, then first aid continues and medical help is sought if needed. Covering the eye or wiping it leaves the chemical in place."),
("Why are colour bowls and mixing tools non-metallic?",
 "Metal can react with the colour", ["Metal bowls are hard to clean", "Plastic keeps colour warmer", "Metal stains the brush bristles"],
 "Some metals react with oxidative colour and peroxide, changing the result and sometimes heating the mix. Non-metallic bowls, brushes and clips avoid that."),
("Clippers run hot and drag after a day of fades. What is done after removing the hair?",
 "Oil the blades", ["Soak the motor in disinfectant", "Wrap the blades in a towel", "Rinse the head under the tap"],
 "Debris is brushed out and the blades are disinfected and re-oiled for smooth running. Soaking or rinsing the powered head damages the motor."),
("A blow dryer's motor strains and the air feels weak. What is checked first?",
 "The intake filter", ["The heat setting", "The nozzle shape", "The diffuser fit"],
 "The RSOS has debris removed from the dryer filter for best performance. A clogged filter starves the motor of air and overheats it."),
("Shears have gone dull and fold the hair. Who restores the edge?",
 "A professional sharpener", ["The stylist on a whetstone", "The salon owner", "Any hardware store machine"],
 "Cutting tools are sharpened and repaired by a professional technician to keep the edge geometry. A home stone or a general grinder can ruin a convex edge."),
]
